  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 1200 AM MDT Wed Oct 7 2026\n\n\nThursday, another dry day is expected. The only change is that it \nmay be a degree or two warm on Thursday as compared to today. Friday \nwill be ditto to Thursday, with maybe another 1 degree or two \nincrease in temperatures.\n\nSaturday, the main change this day will be in the mountains. As for \nthe plains, Saturday will be nearly identical to Friday. \nHowever, over the higher terrain, more clouds are anticipated \nand there will be a better chance of showers over the Divide, \nand likewise, temps will be several degrees cooler over the \nhigher terrain. \n\nOn the large scale, the pattern over the region will change as flow \naloft will shift to a southwesterly direction through most of the \ncolumn as a strong trough moves into the northwestern CONUS and \nbegins to dig southward down the Pacific coast.\n\nBy midday Sunday, the trough over the west coast becomes a full \nlongitude trough along the entire coast as the main Pacific \ntrough interacts/merges with tropical cyclone activity off the \nMexican coast. Flow over the entire Rocky mountain region \nbecomes south- southwesterly and increases. This will push \nmoisture up into the region and expect quite a few showers to be\noccurring over the Contdvd region on this day. This is clearly \nreflected in the statistical guidance as point forecast for the \nWolf Creek region shows heavy rain occurring during the latter \nSunday/Monday period over the Southwest mountains. The plains on\nthis period will likely remain dry, but temps are expected to \ncool into the upper 70s to lower 80s across the lower terrain.\n\nFrom Monday into next week, there is still quite a bit of \nuncertainty on the track, speed, flow orientation and moisture with \nthis large scale trough. Although all of the long range \ndeterministic guidance shows the trough moving through during the \nmid week period, there is still lofts of uncertainty. As mentioned \nyesterday, confidence is high that it will be getting cooler over \nthe entire region next week and it will be wet over the CONTDVD \nregion, but how cool and wet (white) still need to be determined. \n\nBased on the latest deterministic guidance, the trough should move \nacross the state later on Wednesday. \\/Hodanish",
